 - StoryMap note discovery frontmatter: `story-map-note: true`.
 - StoryMap fenced language: `story-map`.
 - StoryMap configuration keys use camelCase.
+- `map.theme` is the single built-in StoryMap visual theme selector. Supported values are
+  `light | dark | vintage | cyber | atlas`, default `light`. A selected theme coordinates
+  both cartographic styling and StoryMap-owned story chrome; do not create a separate story
+  theme. Markdown semantics and host typography remain host-owned.
+- `layout.mode` controls the spatial relationship between story content and the map.
+  Supported v1 modes are `card | full`, default `card`. Layout is document-owned and must
+  render consistently across standalone React, Obsidian, and Remark/Docusaurus.
+- `card` mode preserves the current floating-card behavior by default and may configure
+  `align: left | center | right`, `widthRatio`, and `heightRatio`.
+- `full` mode keeps the map full-bleed and places the story surface on the configured
+  `left | right` side with `contentRatio`; the shared renderer owns the progressive
+  transparent transition and responsive vertical fallback.
 - `noteFolder` supports one Vault-relative folder and includes subfolders recursively.
 - Folder-generated slide order is controlled only by `order: asc | desc` (default `asc`)
   and `dateField` (default `date-created`).
